From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm-dai: keep the source's channel order on capture

The front end sets the output map of the MFC module to the default
speaker layout, FL FR LS RS for four channels. On SC8280XP the codec DMA
source labels its four channels FL FR FC LS, in order, so the MFC remixes
a four-channel capture: the third input is mixed into the first two
outputs, the fourth input comes out third and the fourth output is
silent. Three channels get no map at all.

Label capture channels in order, 1..n. Two-channel capture keeps the
same map, and playback keeps the default layout. Three- and
four-channel capture changes on every board whose topology allows it,
among them the upstream X1E80100 CRD and Yoga Slim 7x topologies, and
whatever the back end (codec DMA, I2S or TDM); only the SC8280XP VA
codec DMA was tested.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
@@ -219,6 +219,7 @@
 	struct audioreach_module_config cfg;
 	struct device *dev = component->dev;
 	struct q6apm_dai_data *pdata;
+	unsigned int i;
 	int ret;
 
 	pdata = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(component);
@@ -235,7 +236,19 @@
 	cfg.num_channels = runtime->channels;
 	cfg.bit_width = prtd->bits_per_sample;
 	cfg.fmt = SND_AUDIOCODEC_PCM;
-	audioreach_set_default_channel_mapping(cfg.channel_map, runtime->channels);
+	/*
+	 * Capture sources number their channels in order, 1..n (seen with
+	 * SC8280XP's VA codec DMA; other back ends untested). The default map is a
+	 * speaker layout (FL FR LS RS for four channels), against which the MFC
+	 * would mix the third channel into the first two and move the fourth.
+	 */
+	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE) {
+		for (i = 0; i < runtime->channels; i++)
+			cfg.channel_map[i] = PCM_CHANNEL_FL + i;
+	} else {
+		audioreach_set_default_channel_mapping(cfg.channel_map,
+						       runtime->channels);
+	}
 	if (prtd->state) {
 		/* clear the previous setup if any  */
 		q6apm_graph_stop(prtd->graph);
